SUMMARY:4th Prague Symposium on Cancer Metabolism 2025
LOCATION:Plzeňská Campus\, Pelouch Lecture Hall\, Prague\, Czech Republic
DESCRIPTION:Fourth edition of a deliberately small cancer-metabolism meetin
 g run by the CLIP metabolic study group at the Second Faculty of Medicine\
 , Charles University\, co-organised by the Institute of Biotechnology of t
 he Czech Academy of Sciences. The limited-attendance format is the point: 
 it is built for exchange between students\, researchers and clinicians rat
 her than for a large audience. A Seahorse user meeting at BIOCEV followed 
 on 16 October.\n\nWhy it matters for mTOR (★★★): mTOR is not in the 
 programme title\, which is cancer metabolism\, but David Sabatini is a lis
 ted invited speaker and he is one of the five researchers the Atlas tracks
  most closely (48 studies in the corpus). His speaker biography on the sym
 posium page is almost entirely mTOR: the discovery of the kinase\, mTORC1 
 and mTORC2\, and nutrient signalling to mTORC1 through the lysosomal Rag G
 TPases. Notable for the Atlas as the Prague meeting Sabatini spoke at from
  his IOCB Prague base\, alongside the separate Prague Metabolism and Signa
 ling Symposium already curated here.\n\nSpeakers or organisers with a prof
 ile in the Atlas: David M. Sabatini\, Arkaitz Carracedo\n\nConference site
 : https://www.lf2.cuni.cz/en/events/4th-prague-symposium-on-cancer-metabol
 ism\n\nIn Oliver's mTOR Atlas: https://mtor-atlas.org/events/#ev-4th-pragu
 e-symposium-on-cancer-metabolism-2025
